// args: --compile
// A global split definition that does not fit its initializer always aborts,
// but each part was given the clamped slice of the initializer as its value,
// of the wrong length, and compiling a use of it crashed. A global needs a
// value, so this is now an error.
// (Found by fuzzing.)
a~(b:_^2222):=[]; /// error
c~(d:_^1):=[1,2,3];
def main()⇒(a,c,d);
